# A server of two threads on the parts every server is built on, and
# nothing of the OS server's (roadmap memory.md M6, *The model for
# multi-threaded servers*; tests/programs/twin.c): a stack segment for each
# thread, the root's ROOT_SERVE, a lock that records its holder, and a
# policy of its own after a fault, which the root's restart after the
# fault calls on a fresh stack.
program: twin
define: TEST_TWIN
# DOSBox-X checks no stack segment's limit (docs/emulators.md).
emulators: bochs mame
match: contains
timeout: 30
---
twin: thread 2 on a stack of its own: yes; the data's DS: yes
twin: ROOT_SERVE for thread 1: 0
twin: thread 1 faulted; it held the lock: yes
twin: thread 2 woken by the policy: yes; the lock free: yes
twin: done
